# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -2 has a slot for each opponent (CR 601.2c), and a player who has left the game keeps their seat
# (CR 800.4a), so the others keep their places. Bot2's library has exactly its seven cards, so it loses by drawing on turn 2.
# On turn 4 Bot2's slot has nothing to choose (it is not asked) and holds no target, and the question that is asked is Bot3's slot:
# Bot3's Sol Ring is the target and returns to Bot3's hand, still legal as the ability resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Island x4
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7

[Bot3 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Island x5
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Cast
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Island.Play
Bot3.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Activate(Ability: For each opponent)
Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
! Bot1.Target
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Status = Lost
Bot3.Battlefield = Island
Bot3.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Sol Ring
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Counters.Loyalty = 1
Stack.Count = 0
